hi i'm riya and this is my recipe for  chocolate tart  one of my favorite dessert is the tart  they can seem really intimidating but i  wanted to show you how easy it was to  make  make sure butter and egg is room  temperature because if you use room  temperature butter with cold eggs they  don't mix well together when you mix  butter and egg you can use hand mixer or  whisk but once you add flour you should  switch to spatula because you don't want  to create a lot of gluten because the  cookie dough will become tough and hard  if you over mix some baking recipes say  to leave the butter at room temperature  but they don't mention that eggs should  also be room temperature which is very  important in recipes like this one  you also want to rest the dough for 30  minutes so it relaxes the gluten and  also the dough is really soft so you  want to make the butter a little harder  and it's easier to roll it out if the  dough breaks when you're molding it it's  okay you can patch it with leftover  dough make sure to poke holes so that  the dough doesn't poof up if you make  something difficult to make and you make  it really well it can boost your  confidence so this tour is great for any  beginner cooks who wants to challenge  themselves a little bit also i use the  instant coffee in this recipe because it  kind of gives a nice bitterness and a  flavor that balances out with the  sweetness of the chocolate so that the  tart doesn't become overly sweet but if  you don't like coffee you can totally  skip this step and it will work just  fine it's just a flavor preference when  you're pouring wet ingredients into the  chocolate pour everything at once then  count 30 seconds and then start mixing  it makes really nice shiny chocolate  filling  also make sure to use good quality dark  chocolate because this recipe is very  simple so quality is very important so  when you bake it make sure to take the  tar out  when the center part is slightly  jiggling because if you overcook it the  chocolate filling start cracking shake a  little bit and if the center slightly  jiggled that is when you have to take  out from the oven this recipe i learned  from a pastry chef i used to work with  at the restaurant in l.a so it's totally  restaurant quality dessert and you can  impress anyone who loves chocolate this  chocolate tar is silky and rich so you  will be satisfied just like  tiny slice this recipe seems a little  bit challenging but if you follow step  by step you can totally make it and you  will be impressed by yourself impress  yourself first and impress other people  next  and it's totally worth that  thank you  i cannot be alex  so a few years ago there was a trend  where you roll up apple slices onto a  pie sheet and made a little tart so i  was wondering if there was anything i  could make that would look pretty like  that and i came up with this idea using  crepes instead of paishi i wasn't sure  if it's gonna work first but i tried it  anyways and when i think of crepes my  favorite feeling is strawberry and  whipped cream so instead of apples i  decided to use strawberries  the important thing about making crepes  is rest the dough for at least 30  minutes because we are mixing with milk  and flour which creates gluten and you  don't want to make chewy and rubbery  crepes  if you want you can also rest it  overnight and make it the next day i  chose cream cheese filling because it's  a little thicker so easy to work with  you are ending up making a bunch of  crepes for this recipe and that will  take time but i also think it's fun as  well so i tested this and made a pretty  small version that was really really  cute  but when i make dessert i usually want  to share so i don't want to make it just  for myself  when you're making a home it's a little  bit messy because you're spreading cream  onto the crepe and rolling it up but  it's worth the effort and it was a mess  because it's really pretty and i'm sure  whoever you're going to give it to will  be super impressed  make sure to cut the strawberries very  thin it's similar to a crepe cake  because it's layered but just a  different presentation because the  crepes are vertical instead of  horizontal  so instead of stopping making small  little tart i was just kept rolling and  rolling and rolling and i ended up  making a large crepe cake i think  rolling it up it's the most fun and  difficult part because it's kind of like  building a snowman it's the same cake  all the way through it just gets bigger  also after you make this rolled crepe  big enough then you can start layering  it on the side instead of rolling them  what you end up with is a super pretty  rolled of crepes all standing up with  strawberries kind of looking like a  flower which is why i called this a rose  crepe cake this is a perfect dessert to  bring on afternoon tea party or just to  make with your friends sometime  [Music]  i was filming this recipe late at night  because i wasn't sure if it's gonna work  so i was kind of testing and shooting at  the same time and alex and scott was  also shooting leia night so we shared  together and both of them are super  impressed so this recipe is something  i'm really proud of because i've never  seen this type of cake before  so i would like you to make it and i  also want you to be proud of it  [Music]  so this recipe was kind of assigned to  me by alden so he made a multi-flavor  sheep pan pie video and we as a team  wanted to see what else can we make  multi-flavor i wanted to make something  easy like i didn't want to make each  flavor from scratch so i wanted to make  one cookie dough and add in different  flavors  [Music]  using brown sugar is very important in  order to give the cookie that chewy  texture that i like  and also using a little white sugar  helps giving a crispy texture  it's good to combine both it's important  to use two type of sugar to make this  american style cookie i feel like  chocolate chip cookie is very unique to  america i feel like this chocolate chip  cookie it's a little bit rustic shape  each individual cup gives a different  shape and kind of i don't know like i  feel like it's imperfect but this  imperfection make it perfect  we kind of came up with simple flavor  combinations that everyone likes like  chocolate chip cookie and peanut butter  and white chocolate macadamia nuts which  is something that's underrated i think  [Music]  i think it's the best multi-flavor  skillet cookie recipe out there i don't  know how many out there  [Music]  i used parchment paper to bake so i can  take it out and transport it to a plate  but if you just want to serve in a  skillet you can do so you don't need to  use the parchment paper each cookie is  next to each other based on how well  their flavor profile combined and of  course everyone wants to eat the middle  part because you can eat whole flavor so  each of six different flavors all in one  cookie  [Music]  and also i cut it in a pea seed so you  can enjoy different flavor combinations  like chocolate chip cookie with peanut  butter cookie and a white chocolate  macadamia cookie with double chocolate  cookies  [Music]  and i think this cookie does a good job  of capturing a lot of different  characters it's difficult to make  imperfect perfect cookie like if you  have american chocolate chip cookie it  kind of has a crack and chocolate chip  is sometimes not evenly distributed  it may have a dent somewhere but it's  cute in a way a whole imperfection makes  a great cookie perfect  it's not something you can intend it to  make it that way but it happens that way  but it's perfect in the way not sure if  you get it i  feel like i'm talking about cookie  philosophy  i don't know i think you just try make  it and maybe you understand what i'm  talking about  [Music]  so i was looking on the internet and  found this really cool cookie called the  shakashaka cookies shakashaka is  onomatopoeia for shaking noise in  japanese so when you shake something and  make noise that is shakashaka the person  made two cookies glued together and put  sprinkles inside so when you shake it  you can see the sprinkles inside moving  and it was very cute the recipe doll  looks very complicated they used a  special kind of sugar called palatinos  which is not sold in regular grocery  stores so i wanted to make it but make  it very simple so everyone can make a  home that's something i always wanted to  include in my video that something  everyone can make a home that's the  great thing about tasty i think and  making this cookie was very fun i made  this video for tasty junior initially  and i had the opportunity to work with  kids  it was very fun to cook with little  girls especially as a child actor i  walked to it she was so impressed  she told me i could be a chef in the  future and i should open the restaurant  and it was very cute and sweet  i was thinking maybe i could use  strawberry candy and melt it there is  also another cookie called the stained  glass cookie which is very popular  so i used the jolly launcher instead of  the special sugar and took two cookies  together with white chocolate so it  tastes better  when i was reading comment i saw some  audience said jolly launcher is too hard  so if you buy into it you might break  your teeth  but when you bake a jolly launcher  spread very thinly so don't worry about  breaking a teeth  you won't break your teeth i'm looking  for you  this video became viral and i saw a lot  of people make it  i also saw some people made it for a  bake sale and it's a great feeling when  someone actually make it and have fun  with it  i think also shakashaka cookies is a  cute name for japanese cookie but if you  translate it it's become shake shape  cookie which is not so catchy  it was our general manager ashley who  was sitting next to me and said oh that  looks like an aquarium so that's why i  named it so don't be afraid of breaking  your teeth  it's actually tasty kids love that and  you can customize it you can put love  letter in it and make it fancy make it  fancy  make it fancy  [Music]  [Applause]  you
 

